WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.990
I get lots of comments and questions if Game
of Thrones prequel series is cancelled.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.340
People say they are reading about it all over
the internet. The answer is yes, one Game

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.230
of Thrones prequel is cancelled, its name
was the Long Night or the Bloodmoon,

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.220
but the other Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.689
about which I've been talking about on this
channel, is not.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:36.800
The game of Thrones prequel series, House
of the Dragon, is in the process of filming

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.739
and will be released early on in 2022, or
in other words in just over one year.

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:48.250
Unlike the Long Night prequel, HBO ordered
the entire first season of House of the Dragon,

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.830
meaning that this prequel cannot be canceled.
HBO's prequel Bloodmoon was meant to fill

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.890
the gap that Game of Thrones left behind,
but the project has been canceled and replaced

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.830
with House of the Dragon. If the Long Night
prequel wasn't canceled, it would already

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:07.990
be out as 2020 was its official release date.
Bloodmoon was supposed to be about the Long

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:13.680
Night. At first, it seemed as if everything
was going just fine with it and HBO even filmed

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.180
a pilot, but for whatever reason, chose not
to turn it into a series. A pilot episode

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:24.820
was written and produced by Jane Goldman,
set thousands of years before Game of Thrones.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.370
Hours after announcing that the Blood Moon
prequel was cancelled,

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.409
HBO announced that they ordered the entire
first season of House of the Dragon.

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:35.950
"Pilots – sometimes they come together,
sometimes they don’t,"

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:41.140
HBO's president Casey Bloys told Variety about
why the network decided to go with one prequel

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.120
series over the other. "And I would say that
was very much the case here.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.890
There’s nothing I would point to and say
"Oh, this was the problem.'"

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:53.170
However, Bloys did reveal that since House
of the Dragon is based on Martin's writing,

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:57.310
it was easier for the show's creative team
to delve into the story of House Targaryen.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:02.600
"That prequel was 8,000 years before the current
show, so it required a lot more invention,"

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.940
he explained. “One of the benefits of 'House
of the Dragon' is there was a text from George

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:13.760
and there was a little bit more of a roadmap."
Set more than 5,000 years before Game of Thrones,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.150
the canceled show Bloodmoon was not planning
to feature any of the Game of Thrones characters

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.790
we already know and love.
As a matter of fact some of the houses and

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:27.269
families did not even exist in this time period,
like Targaryens for example. According to

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:32.189
HBO's official synopsis, the Bloodmoon was
meant to tell the story of "the world's descent

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:35.510
from the golden Age of Heroes into its darkest
hour."

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.530
It planned to centre around the Children of
the Forest and how they created the first

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.779
White Walker we now know as the Night King.
A teaser for the series said it would reveal

00:02:44.779 --> 00:02:50.170
the “horrifying secrets of Westeros’s
history to the true origin of the White Walkers”.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:54.860
The Age of Heroes is the name given to the
period in time which saw the First Men and

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:00.029
the Children of the Forest come together to
agree on a peace pact. This happened around

00:03:00.029 --> 00:03:04.049
10,000 years before the first Game of Thrones
episode is set.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:08.810
It ended around 7,000 years later with the
Coming of the Andals. The exact time the Age

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:14.400
of Heroes ended is not clear as different
sources in Westeros gave different accounts.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.549
This meant that the fans would not know for
sure when the Bloodmoon was set –

00:03:18.549 --> 00:03:22.739
the only details confirmed were that it's
the Age of Heroes era.

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:27.609
Casey Bloys, the President of HBO Programming,
told Deadline: "One of the things I think

00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:32.610
Jane took on beautifully, which was a challenge,
there was a lot more world creation because

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:38.120
she set hers 8,000 years before the original
show, so it required a lot more.'' He added:

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.390
"We would have been very lucky to do one pilot,
have that pilot go and be a success, but in

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:48.499
development as you know, it takes a lot of
tries to get it right. This is no different."

00:03:48.499 --> 00:03:52.400
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
the creator George R.R Martin stated that

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:58.019
Bloodmoon prequel was supposed to be set roughly
5,000 years before the events of Game of Thrones.

00:03:58.019 --> 00:04:03.090
"We are dealing with a different and older
world," Martin told EW.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:08.019
In the interview George R.R Martin also said
"Westeros is a very different place." King's

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:13.040
Landing will not even exist yet, and as a
result, there's no Iron Throne, either. Meanwhile,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.019
Valyria will have "hardly begun to rise,"
Martin explained. "it's not the story we think

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:22.860
we know." It will teach us more about Westeros
history, the white walkers origins, and "the

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.350
mysteries of the East." In his interview with
The New York Times, Martin stressed that the

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.300
Long Night prequel was "mostly" the creation
of Jane Goldman.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:35.480
In his own words: "If you look at the published
books so far, there's really very little material

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:40.111
about the Age of Heroes and the Long Night
— a sentence here, a sentence there. Old

00:04:40.111 --> 00:04:45.870
Nan tells a tale that takes up a paragraph.
So Jane had to create the characters, the

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.300
settings and some of the events,
and we had to look at everything that was

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.009
said and say, 'O.K., here’s what was said
at this point, we need to make it consistent

00:04:54.009 --> 00:04:58.710
to that.' We kicked around some ideas and
I made some suggestions. But mostly it's been

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:04.280
Jane running with it." Martin therefore explained
that he did not create the plot outline, characters,

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:11.380
or setting details for the Long Night TV series.
It was announced by HBO on October 29, 2019

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.889
that plans to produce the Long Night spin
off had been scrapped. After viewing the pilot,

00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:20.650
HBO was not "thrilled by the results" and
even gave showrunner Jane Goldman and her

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:25.360
team notes on changes needed,
but even after the re-edit of the pilot HBO

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:30.720
was still "not thrilled" and decided not to
green light the pilot to series. Hours after

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:35.620
the cancellation that same day, HBO green
lighted instead another Game of Thrones prequel

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:41.099
direct to series that's co-created by George
R.R. Martin &amp; Ryan Condal.

00:05:41.099 --> 00:05:45.470
Condal will be a co-showrunner with famous
Game of Thrones director Miguel Sapochnik

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:50.110
who will also work on the pilot and additional
episodes in the prequel series called House

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:55.689
of the Dragons. House of the Dragon will draw
from George R.R. Martin's novel Fire &amp; Blood,

00:05:55.689 --> 00:05:59.050
which reveals more about the history of the
Targaryens.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:03.640
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.729
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:13.180
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.590
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:20.620
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.919
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:06:24.919 --> 00:06:29.530
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.909
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:06:34.909 --> 00:06:39.000
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.919
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:50.120
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.530
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
Some would think that you could just read

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:59.439
the book Fire &amp; Blood to know what will happen
in the show based on that very same book but

00:06:59.439 --> 00:07:04.090
thats far from truth. Why?
Beacuse Fire And Blood is not a non conventional

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:09.610
novel, it is imaginary history book, and according
to George RR Martin himself, not very accurate

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.620
at that.
Because while Fire And blood book was written

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:18.099
by George RR Martin, it wasn't written from
him as facts, but rather through the perspective

00:07:18.099 --> 00:07:23.350
of the Citadel's Archmaester Gyldayn who gathered
all the info and as many different sources

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:28.669
as he could and used it to write a book about
the Targaryen history. Some info is fake,

00:07:28.669 --> 00:07:33.259
some info is true, some info is semi true.
No one will know for a fact what was happening

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:49.210
in the real history until the House 

00:07:49.210 --> 00:08:24.310
of the Dragon airs 

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:51.270
in 2022.
The show unlike the book will contain truth,

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:56.370
it will depict what actually happened, not
the changed history, fake or semi true, not

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:00.310
what might or might not have happened.
The key event of House of the Dragon will

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.780
be the Targaryen civil war, the Dance of the
Dragons.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:07.890
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:13.250
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:16.310
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:20.700
Iron Throne. When people started declaring
for one of them or the other, their fight

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:26.391
divided the kingdoms in two. Targaryens fought
Targaryens, bothers fought brothers, dragons

00:09:26.391 --> 00:09:31.320
fought dragons. By the time it was over, thousands
were dead. The conflict would prove to be

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:36.060
incredibly destructive for not only House
Targaryen, but large parts of Westeros as

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:41.340
well. In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's
dragon population, ultimately leading to their

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.990
extinction within a few decades.
They never truly recovered.

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:49.810
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:54.130
majority of these died during the civil war
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began

00:09:54.130 --> 00:10:02.570
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.
Dozens of major battles, even more smaller

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:06.430
battles, and even more betrayals, turncloaks,
and twists.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:10.380
All of that this Game of Thrones prequel show,
House of the Dragon, brings in 2022.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.950
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed
this video and if you did make sure to give

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.390
it a big thumbs up. Hope to see you in the
next one, peace!

